{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/561002-beast-endless-soul-loss-plague","id":561002,"title":"[Beast] Endless Soul-Loss Plague?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-19T12:04:27-07:00","id":561002,"title":"[Beast] Endless Soul-Loss Plague?","content":"Use &quot;You are Meat,&quot; combined with &quot;Fear is Contagious.&quot; Spend satiety on both effects (probably a lot of Satiety on the latter). Lets say you start at 9 Satiety and spend all the way down to 2 Satiety (so the Resolve + Composure roll is at -6). So... You start off inflicting Soul Loss on 9 people. Then everyone who interacts with those 9 people in any meaningful fashion get afflicted with Soul Loss, and so on. Since the duration is permanent, this makes them and anyone further affected permanent carriers of this soul plague?<br /> <br /> Am I reading this right?<br /> <br /> As a side thing, can a Beast &quot;cure&quot; Soul Loss by using another Nightmare on the target and succeeding at the Clash of Wills?<br /> <br /> In retrospect, I think these issues, if they are issues, can be fixed by changing the word &quot;permanent&quot; to &quot;instant.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 06-19-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:13:27-07:00","id":561070,"title":"","content":"Are you reading that right? Not quite. You need to spend 1 satiety per Nightmare, from my reading. So, 1 for the permanent effect of You are Meat, 1 for the spread effect of Fear is Contagious. Though, from the sounds of it, I think its 1 Satiety per meaningful interaction as well. Why else would there be the option to spend more than 1 Satiety on that effect? <br /> <br /> No, you can't cure the effects of permanent soul loss through the whole Nightmares clashing thing. If it could simply be restored with dismissal, it would be mentioned. Instead, the effect clearly says the only way to fix it is with an astral journey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:00:02-07:00","id":562164,"title":"","content":"The multiple Satiety spend on Fear is Contagious is to supply a stacking -1 penalty per point spent to the Resolve + Composure roll to resist the contagion. That's all multiple points of Satiety does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:57:08-07:00","id":563113,"title":"","content":"So based on your statement you have nine points (status High) you need to spend 1 to make it spread for Fear is contagious and the nightmare is You are Meat, which make you soulless. So in this fact you make World War Z if you spent a point on You are Meat. But this would not last long as stated &quot;Nightmare effects normally last one scene.&quot; The condition would linger just not the nightmare that invoked it. Unless I missed something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T11:28:05-07:00","id":563175,"title":"","content":"My reading, which I suspect is also MCN's reading, is that the effects of Satiety Expenditure for Fear Is Contagious apply to the Normal and/or High Satiety effects of the modified Nightmare as appropriate and the Satiety Expenditure effect of the base Nightmare only applies to the initial target(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-21-2015, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}